"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Character>"},{"type":"text","text":" holds words,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<Unicode.Scalar>"},{"type":"text","text":" the same words scalar by scalar, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trie<UInt8>"},{"type":"text","text":" byte strings. Lookup,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"insertion and removal follow the key down from the root, O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"m","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"σ","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") for a key of "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":" symbols"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and at most "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"σ"}]},{"type":"text","text":" children per vertex. A trie answers the queries a hash set cannot: every key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a prefix, whether any key has one, and the longest key that is a prefix of a query."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let words = Trie([\"car\", \"cart\", \"cat\", \"dog\"])","words.contains(\"cat\")                                   \/\/ true","words.elements(withPrefix: \"car\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ [\"car\", \"cart\"]","words.longestPrefix(of: \"carton\").map { String($0) }    \/\/ \"cart\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration visits each key before the keys it is a prefix of. When the symbols are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"text":", each vertex keeps its children sorted, so the keys come in lexicographic order;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"otherwise children come in the order they were first added.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"typ